BitSkim 0.2 - RISC OS 3.x development port

Experimental build. No native RISC OS runtime or hardware validation yet.
See README in the distribution for exact requirements and limitations.

Select a nearby computer, then drag one existing disk file from the Filer
onto the main window, or enter its full RISC OS path and choose Send file.
A manual IPv4 address may include :port. Incoming offers show an editable
save path. Existing files are preserved; old FileCore leafnames are limited
to 10 characters. Preferences are stored in Choices inside !BitSkim.

The icon bar entry restores the window. Menu on the entry opens Preferences.
Use the Quit button to exit. TCP/IP is still active while on the icon bar.
Transfers are unencrypted and sender names are not verified.
